{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"square profile","tex_line_start":393,"tex_line_end":405,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"lemma5.1","pdf_page":"8-9 mapping unverified","derivation_or_objection":"Two inverse branches give density denominator 2sqrt(|a||z-v|); f<=1 gives the envelope. Completing the square bounds the preimage of an interval of length 2rho by two radial intervals of total length <=2sqrt(2rho/|a|).","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"definite pair","tex_line_start":407,"tex_line_end":413,"status":"FALSE","clause_id":"C01-global-diffeomorphism-clause","pdf_page":"9","derivation_or_objection":"The literal claim that the half-open polar chart is a diffeomorphism onto the punctured plane is false: the inverse angle is discontinuous across the seam. Remove one ray (Lebesgue null) and use theta in (0,2pi); the Jacobian 1/(2sqrt(det B)) and density bound pi L/sqrt(det B) then follow unchanged.","repair_reference":"CORRECTIONS C01"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"hyperbolic pair","tex_line_start":415,"tex_line_end":442,"status":"GAP","clause_id":"C03-critical-level-atom","pdf_page":"9-10","derivation_or_objection":"Positive and negative level sets, Jacobian 1/(2sqrt D), original-coordinate tail changes, separate i/i' choices, cutoffs and log envelope all check. The proof omits that {q=v} is two affine lines and hence has probability zero under the joint density; insert this to conclude absolute continuity at the critical value.","repair_reference":"CORRECTIONS C03"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"quadratic concentration","tex_line_start":444,"tex_line_end":471,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"lemma5.4","pdf_page":"10","derivation_or_objection":"Large diagonal uses Lemma5.1. Otherwise ||off(S)||>=L/2 and a random cut has Frobenius norm >=L/4. Cor4.4(c)+Gaussian smoothing gives coefficient 18.255...<19. Layer cake yields L0=2+2log19 and excludes atoms.","repair_reference":"C02 inherited through Cor4.4"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"kernel integrals and rearrangement","tex_line_start":473,"tex_line_end":491,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"lemma5.5","pdf_page":"10-11","derivation_or_objection":"The three elementary antiderivatives give the exact J(d) formula for 0<d<=1; concavity bounds the product by 4, d>1 compares to d=1, and centered interval superlevel sets prove the rearrangement inequality.","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"pair half-potential","tex_line_start":493,"tex_line_end":510,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"lemma5.6-after-local-repairs","pdf_page":"11","derivation_or_objection":"Bounded density gives 2sqrt(2M). Definite branch is <6D^-1/4. Indefinite scaling produces h(y)=6+log_+(16/|y|); rearrangement on delta=1/64 gives 12+5log2<16. Depends on locally repaired Lemmas5.2-5.3.","repair_reference":"C01,C03 inherited"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"pivot parameters","tex_line_start":513,"tex_line_end":527,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"definition6.1-small-entry","pdf_page":"11","derivation_or_objection":"No pivot implies |a_ii|<1/12 and a_ij^2<eta^2+zeta=25/2304=(5/48)^2.","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"cross dilation","tex_line_start":529,"tex_line_end":539,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"lemma6.2","pdf_page":"11","derivation_or_objection":"A-DAD=2C entrywise. For C=[[0,M],[M^T,0]], each nonzero singular value of M gives eigenvalues +/-sigma, so singular values of C are doubled.","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"Rademacher second moment","tex_line_start":541,"tex_line_end":558,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"lemma6.3","pdf_page":"11-12","derivation_or_objection":"Only ordered pairs (p,q)=(i,j),(j,i) survive sign averaging. Frobenius inner products give the two displayed terms; Cauchy-Schwarz and |o_ij|<=a yield the 2a^2(sum|phi_i|^2)^2 bound.","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"random-sign crossing","tex_line_start":560,"tex_line_end":580,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"proposition6.4","pdf_page":"12","derivation_or_objection":"Compression to k=2m-1 eigenvectors, diagonal/off-diagonal split and a sign choice with Frobenius error <sqrt2 a0 k give s_k(2Phi^TC Phi)>2gamma_m. Compression plus doubled singular values gives s_m(A_IJ)>gamma_m; E_m then exceeds gamma_m^(2m).","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"no-pivot density/half-potential","tex_line_start":582,"tex_line_end":596,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"proposition7.1","pdf_page":"12-13","derivation_or_objection":"m=3 gives E3>gamma3^6 and density <15/gamma3<167. m=2 gives E2>gamma2^4 and half-potential <12.2/sqrt(gamma2)<26. Depends on repaired C02.","repair_reference":"C02 inherited"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"global three-direction half-potential","tex_line_start":598,"tex_line_end":616,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"proposition7.2","pdf_page":"13","derivation_or_objection":"No-pivot branch is <26; pair pivot gives 16 zeta^-1/4=64; diagonal pivot uses the Schur complement with two surviving large eigenvalues, Lemma5.4 no-atoms/log moment, J(d), and a tail <=1 to obtain <77.","repair_reference":"C01,C02,C03 inherited as dependencies"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"main theorem proof","tex_line_start":618,"tex_line_end":639,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"theorem1.1-proof-after-local-repairs","pdf_page":"13","derivation_or_objection":"No pivot <167. Diagonal pivot loses one spectral direction and uses Proposition7.2: sqrt12*77<267. Definite pair <16pi<51. Indefinite pair loses two directions; concentration of the Schur critical value and sup D^-1/2 log_+D=2/e give <269. Scaling Y=KX gives K^2/s.","repair_reference":"C01,C02,C03 inherited"}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"half-potential scaling remark","tex_line_start":641,"tex_line_end":643,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"remark7.3","pdf_page":"13","derivation_or_objection":"Scaling gives 77K/sqrt(s). Uniform[0,1] and Q=X_1^2 has infinite E|Q|^-1/2, so one large eigenvalue cannot suffice.","repair_reference":null}
{"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","account":"account01","slot":"B06","run_id":"20260925T003702Z-account01-B06-five-sv-audit-r1","pass_id":"pass1","statement_label":"four-eigenvalue crossing limitation","tex_line_start":645,"tex_line_end":647,"status":"PASS","clause_id":"remark7.4","pdf_page":"13-14","derivation_or_objection":"Each star block has eigenvalues +/-1; direct sum gives 1,1,-1,-1. N>256 removes all stated pivots. For every cut each star contributes rank<=1 to A_IJ, hence total rank<=2 and E3=0. This limits the order-three crossing method only.","repair_reference":null}
